file=Legal & Compliance/scribe/logical/book-requirements.md · h=agent: scribe\ndepartment: Legal & Compliance\ntype: logical-book-requirements\ntouch: 1                       # placeholder — books identified, no extraction yet (playbook §8.1)\ntouch_2_status: pending\nlast_updated: 2026-07-29\n · s·l:scribe \· logical / book-requirements=> **Touch 1 placeholder** (playbook §8.1). Records candidate books identified via the §8.12 end-of-agent step and the §8.8a 3-attempt free-source hunt. No scripts have been extracted yet; every 0.6-flagged judgment below is currently reasoning-based (§0.6) and stays flagged until touch 2 runs.\n\n · psf:Proposed scripts for touch-2 (§8.0 minimum-two-books-per-script)=Path chosen 2026-07-29: **Path 1 — all-free build.** No paywalled books required to reach Tier A (§8.4).\n · tb=\| # \| Proposed script \| Route \| Source book #1 (★) \| Source book #2 \| Notes \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| 1 \| `contract_drafting_method` \| B \| Adams & Cramer — *A Practical Guide to Drafting Contracts: From Concept to Closure* (CALI eLangdell, 2nd ed. 2024) — [CALI](https://www.cali.org/the-elangdell-bookstore) \| UNIDROIT — *Principles of International Commercial Contracts (2016)* — [Official PDF](https://www.unidroit.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Unidroit-Principles-2016-English-bl.pdf) \| Grounds `contract-library` classification schema and F/G/E edit-boundary discipline; grounds `contract-review-routing` playbook categories. Likely `.py` for enumerated rules + `.md` for style guidance. \| · tb=\| 4 \| `contract_obligation_taxonomy` \| B \| Adams & Cramer — *A Practical Guide to Drafting Contracts* (CALI eLangdell, 2nd ed. 2024) \| UNIDROIT — *Principles of International Commercial Contracts (2016)* \| Grounds `obligation-extraction` Step 2 with a real, book-sourced 10-type taxonomy + pattern rules. **Replaces the invented script deleted 2026-07-29** (see "Corrections" below). Must produce Route B rule engine with self-tests per §5.2 and §8.0. \| · tb=\| 2 \| `contract_doctrine_unidroit` **✅ EXTRACTED touch-2 2026-07-29** — `Shared OS/logical/contract_doctrine_unidroit.py` (Route B — 18 verbatim UNIDROIT articles, doctrine-tag registry, contract-scanner) \| B/C \| UNIDROIT Principles 2016 (institutional, free) — [Official PDF](https://www.unidroit.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Unidroit-Principles-2016-English-bl.pdf) \| CISG (UN Convention 1980, free UNCITRAL) \| · tb=\| 2b \| `contract_doctrine_us` (still pending) — US common-law counterpart to script #2 \| B/C \| Snyder & Burge — *American Contract Law for a Global Age* (Texas A&M Law) — [Open Textbook Library](https://open.umn.edu/opentextbooks/textbooks/596) \| American Law Institute — *Restatement (Second) of Contracts* — [Internet Archive](https://archive.org/details/restatementoflaw0012unse) (controlled digital lending) \| US-doctrine mirror of the UNIDROIT-grounded script; touch-2 pending \| · tb=\| 3 \| `negotiation_judgment` \| D \| *Negotiation Journal* (40 years open access) — MIT Press / Harvard PON — [PON](https://www.pon.harvard.edu/daily/teaching-negotiation-daily/negotiation-journal-now-open-access/) \| Arthur Corbin — *Corbin on Contracts* (One Volume Edition) — [Internet Archive](https://archive.org/details/corbinoncontract0000arth) (controlled digital lending) \| Grounds `vendor-agreement-review` redline granularity and cap-carveout logic; grounds `scribe-principles` ambiguity-→-ASK rule. §8.9 Route D — mostly `.md` for qualitative extraction, `.py` for any quantifiable heuristics (e.g., concession patterns). \| · psf:Proposed scripts for touch-2 (§8.0 minimum-two-books-per-script)=**Tier assessment (§8.4):** all 3 proposed scripts are Tier A candidates (real book supplied) → flag removable on touch-2.\n\n**Source authentication (§8.8):**\n- **Institutional:** UNIDROIT (intergovernmental), American Law Institute (professional academy), MIT Press (academic publisher).\n- **Academic:** Adams & Cramer (CALI eLangdell — Indiana University McKinney), Snyder & Burge (Texas A&M), Charles Fried (Harvard), Arthur Corbin (Yale historical).\n- **No unauthenticated sources.** No blog posts, no vendor whitepapers, no summary sites.\n\n**Whole-book access (§8.10):** UNIDROIT + PON journal are direct-PDF/full-web-access. CALI books require free email registration. Open Textbook Library is direct. Internet Archive uses controlled digital lending (borrow one at a time) — that is whole-book access, just queued. No summary-site substitution permitted.\n\n · is:Inherited scripts=None yet. `Shared OS/logical/` is currently empty of scribe-relevant scripts. If a future logical script (e.g. contract-drafting method) is extracted for another Legal & Compliance agent first, scribe imports it rather than duplicating (playbook §13.1, §13.5).\n\n · tb=\| Skill \| Imports from `Shared OS/logical/` (touch-2) \| Rationale \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| `contract-review-routing` \| `contract_drafting_method` \· `contract_doctrine` \| Playbook categories (script #1); jurisdiction-delta check (script #2) \| · tb=\| `vendor-agreement-review` \| `contract_doctrine` \· `negotiation_judgment` \| Cap-carveout + redline granularity (script #3); Restatement §-lookups (script #2) \| · tb=\| `contract-library` \| `contract_drafting_method` \| Classification schema + edit-boundary marks \| · tb=\| `obligation-extraction` \| `contract_obligation_taxonomy` (script #4, pending touch-2) \| Deterministic 10-type taxonomy + pattern rules replacing current LLM-based Step 2 \| · fc(:Flag clearance (0.6 audit — playbook §8.5)=Current state: **all scribe judgments below are reasoning-based** (0.6-flagged) pending touch-2.\n · tb=\| Judgment \| Skill(s) \| Current state \| Cleared by (touch-2) \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| Cap-carveout materiality assessment \| `vendor-agreement-review` \| reasoning-based \| script #3 (`negotiation_judgment`) — Tier A after extraction \| · tb=\| Jurisdiction-delta enforceability call \| `vendor-agreement-review` \| reasoning-based, book-citable at Tier B (canonical statutes named in skill body) \| script #2 (`contract_doctrine`) — Tier A \| · tb=\| Deal-breaker prioritisation \| `vendor-agreement-review`, `contract-review-routing` \| reasoning-based \| script #1 (`contract_drafting_method`) + operator config \| · tb=\| Agreement type classification \| `contract-review-routing` (Step 3) \| heuristic (title + first-page signals) \| script #1 — Tier A after extraction \| · tb=\| F/G/E edit-boundary marks per clause \| `contract-library` (Step 3) \| reasoning-based (operator judgment) \| script #1 — Tier A after extraction \| · tb=\| SMB 8-category classification \| `contract-library` (Step 2) \| schema-based; classification of specific clauses is judgment \| script #1 — Tier A after extraction \| · tb=\| Obligation-candidate type classification \| `obligation-extraction` (Step 2) \| **LLM-based reasoning** (invented script deleted 2026-07-29) + operator judgment \| script #4 (`contract_obligation_taxonomy`) — Tier A after touch-2 \| · c(:Corrections (2026-07-29)=- **Invented script removed.** During the initial build I wrote `scripts/extract_obligations.py` inside `obligation-extraction/` — pattern-matching regex authored from general knowledge, not extracted from a source book. This violated:\n- **§13.5** — all logical scripts belong in `Shared OS/logical/`, not under an agent's `custom/<skill>/scripts/`.\n- **§0.5** — no invented values; the patterns were my invention, not from a book.\n- **§8** — the `logical/` folder is for judgments *grounded in a real source, never invented from general knowledge*.\n- The script and its `scripts/` folder were deleted. `obligation-extraction` Step 2 is now LLM-based extraction, tagged `[REASONING-BASED]` per §0.6 until the real script (row 4 above) is produced by touch-2.\n- **Touch-2 must produce `contract_obligation_taxonomy.py`** at `Shared OS/logical/`, sourced from Adams & Cramer + UNIDROIT, with self-tests per §5.2 and two-book minimum per §8.0. Only then does the reasoning flag on `obligation-extraction` come off.\n\n · sp:Still pending=- **Touch-2 extraction itself.** All four scripts named above are candidates, not code. Extraction runs when the operator schedules it.\n- **Ken Adams — *A Manual of Style for Contract Drafting* (ABA, paywalled).** Not on Path 1. If the operator later drops this in `Agents/_books/`, extract in touch-2 as a third source for script #1 (`contract_drafting_method`) — it's the industry-standard drafting-conventions reference and would strengthen the script beyond Path 1's already-Tier-A grounding.\n- **Tina L. Stark — *Drafting Contracts: How & Why Lawyers Do What They Do* (Wolters Kluwer, paywalled).** Same treatment — optional extra Route D source if operator supplies.\n\nEvery proposed script above stays Tier A even without those two — the pending list is enrichment, not a blocker.\n